repository-code: 'https://github.com/syncytium2/murderboard'
url: 'https://github.com/syncytium2/murderboard'
abstract: >-
  A project-neutral adversarial review process for document
  deliverables — explainers, methods text, figures and their
  captions, reports, handoffs — together with the gates that
  keep it honest. Eleven reviewer roles check every claim
  against a real source, verify every citation, and run the
  mechanical checks against a rendered artifact rather than
  its generator. What distinguishes it from a review prompt is
  that the review is itself gated: a derived roster verifies
  from the finished report that every role actually ran, a
  freshness gate reports when a vendored copy has fallen
  behind upstream, and a severity floor with a round cap makes
  the verify loop terminate. Distributed by vendoring rather
  than dependency; each copy carries a provenance stamp that
  the freshness gate reads.
keywords:
  - peer review
  - document review
  - large language models
  - AI agents
  - research software
  - reproducibility
  - scientific writing
  - claude code
